From ccdd261e10dea4464f27383e5a88d752f8237973 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cpkt9762 <cpkt9762@163.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:00:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(store): re-push already-synced records after a project
 rename

Project backfill previously deduplicated on entity_key and source without
checking whether acknowledged entries represented the current project.
After a rename, that suppressed fresh upserts for already-synced records.

Only acknowledged entries under the current project count as coverage.
Unacknowledged pending and quarantined entries still cover the entity
across project names, because the upstream identity migration moves them.
Keep scoped detectors, enrolled-project discovery and backfill predicates
aligned; leave delete-tombstone coverage unchanged.

Never rewrite acknowledged journal history: the upstream contract in
internal/store/project_canonicalization_test.go requires it to remain
immutable. Instead, backfill new upserts from current entity rows, so an
old payload cannot overwrite newer content imported from a peer.

Regression tests cover migration and ordinary MergeProjects, exact history
preservation, current payloads, pending/quarantined deduplication and
idempotent backfill. Both predicate-removal and history-rewrite mutations
fail the intended tests; the upstream explicit-merge test remains intact.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6.1-sol) <noreply@openai.com>
